# W2.4h, review 38's first finding on a stock client: a world stream belongs to one load, and a newer load fences
# it. The server deflates maze's streams 8 s late (shard.debug.stream-delay), so alpha's /sync of maze is still being
# deflated when its /world transfer loads fortress; that late stream must never reach the client. It also shows that
# each path that resends a world (/sync, the transfer) sends worldDataBegin first: the client counts the worlds it
# loads (vanilla fires WorldLoadEvent for each) and reads the map it shows, through the js probe.
#
#   rig/run.sh --push server/build/install/shard --clients 1 --script rig/scenarios/shard-loads.rig \
#     --server 'SHARD_OPTS=-Dshard.debug.stream-delay=maze=8s "$RIG"/vm/shard-server.sh maze fortress'
timeout 6m

# the server trains its AOT cache first (shard-l5.sh), about a minute
wait port 240s
alpha: join nounit
wait log server /\(alpha\) has connected to maze/ 30s
alpha: expect js "var loads = 0; Events.on(WorldLoadEvent, function(e){ loads++; }); 'counting'" /^counting$/
alpha: expect js "Vars.state.map.name()" /^Maze$/

# /sync alone: worldDataBegin, then maze again, 8 s late
alpha: chat "/sync"
alpha: expect js "loads" /^1$/ 30s
alpha: expect js "Vars.state.map.name()" /^Maze$/
alpha: expect connected
wait 6s

# /sync, then /world while maze's stream is still deflating. The client shows the loading screen after the
# sync's worldDataBegin, so it sends the second command as its chat field would, through Call.sendChatMessage.
alpha: expect js "Call.sendChatMessage('/sync'); 'sent'" /^sent$/
wait 1s
alpha: expect js "Call.sendChatMessage('/world fortress'); 'sent'" /^sent$/
wait log server /\(alpha\) moves from maze to fortress/ 15s
alpha: expect js "Vars.state.map.name()" /^Fortress$/ 30s
alpha: expect js "loads" /^2$/
# maze's late stream is done by now: fenced, it never comes
wait 10s
alpha: expect js "Vars.state.map.name()" /^Fortress$/
alpha: expect js "loads" /^2$/
alpha: expect connected
alpha: shot in-fortress
console players
wait log server /alpha uuid=.* world=fortress state=in_world/ 10s

# and back: maze comes 8 s late again, and nothing fences it this time
alpha: chat "/world maze"
wait log server /\(alpha\) moves from fortress to maze/ 15s
alpha: expect js "Vars.state.map.name()" /^Maze$/ 30s
alpha: expect js "loads" /^3$/
alpha: expect connected
# tick timing is shard-two-clients' and shard-maps' gate; here the server only has to stay error-free
assert log server !/Exception|ERROR/
assert clean all
